                    'A routing rule maps each key to a shard: for example, shard = hash(user_id) % 16.',
                    'The application, or a proxy, uses that rule to send each query to the right shard.',
                    'Queries by user_id hit one shard and are fast. Queries across all users must ask every shard and merge the results, which is slow.',
